<title>UK: Algeria's Skikda port still shut, forecast better.</title>
<headline>Algeria's Skikda port still shut, forecast better.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's Skikda port remained closed on Tuesday due to bad weather but the forecast was better for Wednesday when oil tankers may be allowed to berth, a port official said.</p>
<p>&quot;Possibly this afternoon we will berth a methane carrier but there is still some swell,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The 10 oil tankers waiting outside the port will not berth on Tuesday but possibly on Wednesday, he said.</p>
<p>Naphtha traders said four large tankers able to hold 50,000 to 60,000 tonnes were waiting to be loaded at Skikda, which has been shut for most of the last two weeks.</p>
<p>-- John Hanley, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8185</p>
